{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Brief History of Javascript"}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use these words when talking about the history of JavaScript."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Reads and Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n6le03ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past Statements - Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use <strong>past simple</strong> to talk about actions that started and finished in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use past simple for actions that happened and finished in the past<br/><br/>Structure:<br/><div class=\"center_text\">Subject + verb in past + complement. </div><br/>Example</br><span class=\"italic\">I <b>washed</b> the car last weekend</span><br/><i>The company <b>lost</b> many potential customers.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Microsoft did not want to implement JavaScript in Internet Explorer, but in 2003, they gave up and accepted it."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Jesse James Garret stablished described different technologies, but JavaScript was the backbone of all. JavaScript allowed the creation of dynamic web applications. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past Passive Voice with Frequency Adverbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <strong>simple past in passive voice</strong> to talk about actions that happened in the past but we focus on the event and not in the person who did the action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Passive voice</strong> is used to focus on the action rather on the person or subject that does the action.<br/><br/>We can add an adverb of frequency to make an special focus to the action.<br/><br/>It follows this structure:<br/><div class=\"center_text\">Object + was/were + adverb of frequency + Past participle of the verb + complement.</div><br/><br/> Examples:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <b>was</b>  never <b>given</b>  a bad treat in my travel to Japan.<br/>English <b>was</b> always <b>implemented</b> in the Colombia School curriculums.</span><br/><br/>As you can see, the people behind the actions, Japanese people in the first example and politicians and teachers in the second, are not important, the focus is in the object of the action."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was not always known by the name JavaScript. Its original name was Mocha."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This program was never designed to be perfect since the start."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "baseline "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the starting point for a project "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: ECMAScript 3 in 1999, which is the baseline for the current JavaScript."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le03ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "design"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to plan an event, object or project "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This program was never designed to be perfect since the start."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le03ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rejoin "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " when someone leaves a group and then joins it once again "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Brendan Eich, JavaScript creator, and Mozilla rejoined ECMA and worked in new programming language."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le03ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "converge "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to join or congregate two or more elements "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Their projects were very different from JavaScript, and so they could not be converged."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le03ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "backbone "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the biggest support or pillar of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Jesse James Garret stablished described different technologies, but JavaScript was the backbone of all."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le03ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "party "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group that shares a goal or view e.g. Political party "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The different parties involving programming languages met in Oslo in 2008."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le03ob12aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for more information about the history of JavaScript."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a timeline with the most relev